<title>USA: Results of poll showing prestige of occupations.</title>
<headline>Results of poll showing prestige of occupations.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a table showing how Americans rank occupations in terms of their prestige. The Harris Poll of 1,006 adults was taken between March 26 and April 1.</p>
<p>Occupation	     Prestigious %	 Non-Prestigious %</p>
<p>Doctor			 87			  12</p>
<p>Scientist		    86			  13</p>
<p>Teacher			78			  21</p>
<p>Engineer		     74			  25</p>
<p>Minister/Clergyman	 73			  26</p>
<p>Police officer	     68			  31</p>
<p>Military officer	   66			  33</p>
<p>Member of Congress	 58			  41</p>
<p>Business leader	    58			  41</p>
<p>Lawyer			 52			  47</p>
<p>Banker			 52			  47</p>
<p>Journalist		   51			  48</p>
<p>Accountant		   50			  48</p>
<p>Artist			 50			  49</p>
<p>Athlete			49			  50</p>
<p>Entertainer		  46			  53</p>
<p>Union leader		 39			  59</p>
<p>Source: Harris Poll</p>
</text>
